                <invention-title lang="de">BEFEUCHTUNGSKAMMER FÜR EINE ATEMTHERAPIEVORRICHTUNG</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">CHAMBRE D'HUMIDIFICATION POUR UN APPAREIL DE THÉRAPIE RESPIRATOIRE</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">A HUMIDIFICATION CHAMBER FOR A RESPIRATORY THERAPY APPARATUS</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A flow of gases in a respiratory therapy system can be conditioned to achieve more consistent output from sensors configured to sense a characteristic of the flow. The flow can be mixed by imparting a tangential, rotary, helical, or swirling motion to the flow of gases. The mixing can occur upstream of the sensors. The flow can be segregated into smaller compartments to reduce turbulence in a region of the sensors.</p>
            </abstract>
